<title>BELGIUM: Boeing to make no new exclusive deals for 10 years.</title>
<headline>Boeing to make no new exclusive deals for 10 years.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commissioner Karel Van Miert said on Wednesday that Boeing Co had agreed not to conclude any new exclusive supply contacts with airlines for the next 10 years.</p>
<p>Asked at a news conference to clarify the agreement the Commission had reached with the aircraft manufacturing giant on the supply contracts, Van Miert said:</p>
<p>&quot;That applies for a period of 10 years and that applies to all aspects of exclusivity.&quot;</p>
<p>The contracts had been one of the main sticking points in the negotiations leading to the European Commission's approval in principle on Wednesday of Boeing's takeover of McDonnell-Douglas.</p>
</text>
